      "english": "From a Freudian perspective, a suddenly aging dream connects to the death drive (Thanatos) — the unconscious anxiety about mortality and decay expressing itself through the imagery of aging. The dream may also re-enact complex childhood feelings toward parents or authority figures. Dreaming of oneself aging can reflect an unconscious identification with one's parents or a deep-seated fear of being forced to assume parental roles and responsibilities."
